  lib_plain.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: a lib that does not use the runtime

  A `module lib` is a static library. This one's code never calls into the
  PaskalCPP runtime (no div / mod, guard, raise, sets, ...), so it ships
  alone: no startup hook, no pcpp_runtime beside it, and a C program links it
  with a plain C driver. lib_plain_host.pcpp (PaskalCPP) and lib_plain_host.c
  (C, another toolchain) are its consumers. lib_runtime.pcpp is the other case.
  It builds and is not run: lib_plain_host.pcpp holds the output to expect.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lib_plain.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\lib_plain.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  CHECK: output\lib_plain\lib holds lib_plain.lib and nothing else;
  output\lib_plain_linux\lib holds liblib_plain.a and nothing else.
  Then lib_plain_host.pcpp (a PaskalCPP program that links it).

  A C program built by another toolchain, a C driver, the lib alone:
    res\zig\zig.exe cc -target x86_64-windows-gnu res\tests\lib_plain_host.c output\lib_plain\lib\lib_plain.lib -o output\lib_plain_c.exe
    output\lib_plain_c.exe
    res\zig\zig.exe cc -target x86_64-linux-gnu res\tests\lib_plain_host.c output\lib_plain_linux\lib\liblib_plain.a -o output\lib_plain_c
    wsl ./output/lib_plain_c
  CHECK: both print   from C: lib_plain_add(2, 3) = 5

  Break it (by hand, one step at a time, undo each before the next):
    1. in this file, "AA + AB" -> "AA div AB", then build it (windows) and run
       the C program steps (windows) again.
       CHECK: the build prints "Publishing pcpp_runtime.lib to ...output/lib_plain/lib..."
       and pcpp_runtime.lib now sits beside lib_plain.lib (div calls the runtime);
       the C link fails: lld-link: error: undefined symbol: pcpp::init(int, char**)
       (a runtime-using lib needs pcpp_runtime and a C++ driver: lib_runtime.pcpp).
       Undo: restore the line and build it (windows) again.
       CHECK: it prints "Removed ...output/lib_plain/lib/pcpp_runtime.lib: this
       lib no longer uses the runtime" and lib_plain.lib is alone again
    2. lib_plain_host_err_nolink.pcpp: the host without its @linklibrary line
*******************************************************************************/

module lib lib_plain;
@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
@outputpath "$P:output/lib_plain_linux";
@else
@outputpath "$P:output/lib_plain";
@endif

exported routine clink lib_plain_add(AA: int32; AB: int32): int32;
begin
  return AA + AB;
end;

end.
